        "head_faq": {
          "type": "section_head",
          "settings": {
            "label": "",
            "title": "The questions I get asked most.",
            "align": "center",
            "small": false,
            "tight": false
          }
        },
        "faq1": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Why NAD⁺ rather than any of the other longevity ingredients?",
            "answer": "<p>Because it is upstream of most of them. NAD⁺ is the coenzyme mitochondria use to make energy and repair enzymes need to clear damage, and it declines steadily with age - by your forties you are running on roughly half what you had in your twenties. Raising the input funds both systems rather than pushing on one output.</p>",
            "open_by_default": true
          }
        },
        "faq2": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "You consult for supplement companies. Isn’t this a conflict?",
            "answer": "<p>It is the reason the product exists. Fourteen years of reading other people’s formulations is what showed me where the standard sits and what the category is willing to leave unproven. MUTO is the version I could sign off on, which is a different thing from the version that maximises margin.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "faq3": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What will I feel, and what will I see on my wearable?",
            "answer": "<p>There are no stimulants in it, so nothing in the first hour. Most people describe the afternoon dip going first, in weeks three to four, then steadier mornings. On the device it is slower: HRV and resting heart rate typically start moving between day 30 and day 60, read as a weekly trend rather than a single morning.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "faq4": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "I already take a stack. Does this replace any of it?",
            "answer": "<p>Often two or three products. Every dose is printed in full, so overlap is visible rather than guessed at - most people find the B vitamins, zinc and CoQ10 they were buying separately are already covered here at research-level doses.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "faq5": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What if my data doesn’t move?",
            "answer": "<p>Then send it back. The 90-day guarantee exists because I would rather you judged this on your own numbers than on how the marketing reads. Log your 30-day HRV and resting heart rate average before you start so the comparison means something.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        }
